<p>Aaaand just accidentally closed my window and lost my reply. Reconstructing, the short version.</p>
<p>1) Your redactions don't make me think &quot;what if his brain's a mushroom?&quot; They make me fill them in with silly things like &quot;his opinion on cheese&quot; and &quot;Georgia.&quot;<br />
2) Because you've redacted any potential reference to mushrooms, the third anomalous effect makes no sense at all. I literally skimmed over it without paying attention because it didn't make any sense or add to the story in any way.<br />
3) I nearly downvoted you based on the phrasing in your containment procedures: specifically, the lack of variety. In that section alone, you have</p>
<ul>
<li>Two consecutive sentences that begin &quot;Personnel are warned that SCP-1247&#8230;&quot;</li>
<li>Two consecutive sentences: &quot;&#8230;standard humanoid containment cell. Standard humanoid SCP containment&#8230;&quot;</li>
<li>Three paragraphs that begin with &quot;To ensure psychological stability of SCP-1247&#8230;&quot;</li>
<li>Three consecutive sentences that begin with &quot;Dr Zhang is required to&#8230;&quot;, &quot;Dr Zhang is required to&#8230;&quot;, and &quot;Dr Zhang has emphasized that.&quot;</li>
<li>On top of the above, the name &quot;Dr Zhang&quot; appears in five consecutive sentences (of the six in that paragraph).</li>
</ul>
<p>4) I also nearly downvoted when I saw the name &quot;Shia LaBeouf.&quot; And then it was so bizarre and thorough that I kept reading, and got to the end and didn't want to downvote it anymore.</p>
<p>Please fix the few issues this does have. It's based on a ridiculous Internet meme song and shouldn't work, but somehow it does.</p>

