														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1627021">
									

<p>Ooh, loved ones is a good idea. I'll definitely have a think about that. It's a little more horror than what I've got now, and I'm not quite sure if I've got the horror chops to pull it off, but definitely an excellent suggestion. Still open to others, though!</p>
<p>My original idea was that the guy saw himself as every animal, which would certainly be a mind-mongler. I turned to Shia, as I thought that that, although less traumatic, would mongle minds even more. Eating yourself or a loved one, you would ask &quot;What have I done to deserve this?&quot; and could probably come up with an answer. When it's someone you've never even met, there's no answer, which is all the more monglery.</p>
<p>Dr Adams, the idea of killing the real Labeouf is so blaringly brilliant and frankly obvious that I'm amazed I never even thought of it. The only reason I'm not stealing it is that poor old 3-Black-Boxes would never be able to find the real one. it's like that one awful page in Where's Wally where he's surrounded by Wally clones.</p>
<p>Fridge Logic on the vegetarianism, but the sad truth is that I just considered poor old 3BB to be too dumb to survive in the forest through scavenging alone. He's a bit of a dolt, and the mind-mongling didn't help.</p>
<p>Mongle.</p>
<p><strong>Edit:</strong> azzleflux got in before me on both of Dr Adams's points. Death of the author is not so bad when you hit the nail right on the head!</p>

